menu "Pajoniiir JC1060 BSP (jc4880 shim)"

config BSP_PCM5102A_MAIN_OUT
    bool "Enable PCM5102A main I2S output"
    default y
    help
        Upstream M2.2 gate (audio_engine.c): when enabled the engine takes
        bsp_audio_get_main_i2s_tx() and writes MAIN to the external PCM5102A
        DAC. Without it the main sink is a stub returning
        ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED and playback cannot pace.

config PAJ_MAIN_OUT_USB
    bool "Route MAIN output to the DDJ UAC sink instead of the PCM5102A"
    default n
    help
        When enabled the audio engine still pushes master+phones to the
        DDJ-FLX4 over UAC (4-channel), but the PCM5102A I2S MAIN path is
        withheld (bsp_audio_get_main_i2s_tx() returns NULL). When disabled,
        MAIN plays on the PCM5102A RCA output exactly like upstream M2.2.
        Headphone cue always goes through the DDJ UAC path; the onboard
        ES8311 codec is not used.

endmenu
